WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.002
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.370
You're here!

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.572
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:08.174
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.475
Let's get to some news.

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:12.378 line:0%
Well guys, today was
Judge Ketanji Brown Jackson's

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:15.381 line:0%
final day facing questions
from senators

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:17.350 line:0%
during her confirmation
hearings.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.386
That's right, after nearly
30 hours of questions.

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:21.787
Whew, yeah.

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:24.224
Her husband was so scared to ask
what she wanted for dinner,

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.758
he just ordered
takeout from everywhere.

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:27.426
He's just like,
"Yeah, never mind, never mind.

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:29.229
Do you wanna watch Netflix --
no Netflix, okay.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.897
We'll just put a --
let's buy another TV.

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.198
We'll put on
two things at once."

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.632
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:35.468 line:0%
But this is great --
according to a new poll,

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:38.304 line:0%
Judge Jackson already has
a record approval rating

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:41.374 line:0%
among Americans
for a Supreme Court nominee.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:47.280 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.515
Right now, Biden's like,
"Hey, I nominated you.

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.251
It's only fair we split
that approval rating.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.652
Come on."

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.887
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.221
Yep, the only way
it could have been higher

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.289
is if she ended today
with a water bottle flip.

00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:00.393
It's like, "Oh, yeah!"

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.895 line:0%
In other news, despite the
current state of affairs,

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:06.833 line:0%
Vladimir Putin is still planning
to attend the G20 summit

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.435 line:0%
with other world leaders
in Bali this fall.

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:11.537 line:0%
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:12.872
Which explains
this year's theme...

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.507
"awkward."

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.675
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:16.843
Seriously, what is he doing?

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.077
It's like getting
kicked out of high school

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:19.412
and then showing up
for the reunion.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.114
Like, "What's up, guys?"

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:24.083
"No, you were --No."

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.219
Yeah, it'll backfire on Putin
when he realizes

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.321
it's not a G20 summit,
it's an intervention.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:33.893
He's like, "Wait a minute, I --
I remember you."

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.262 line:0%
Some business news,
apparently Apple has experienced

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:39.866 line:0%
two major outages
in the past two days.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.135
Luckily, the problem was fixed
when the guy at the Genius Bar

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:45.338
told Tim Cook to just drop the
entire company in a bag of rice.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:50.610
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.145
Yeah, in the most recent outage,

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:55.381
Apple Music and Apple Books
went down,

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.015
which means no one noticed.

00:01:57.015 --> 00:01:59.352
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.954
Apple Books?

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.791
"Hey,
look it up on Apple Books."

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:10.063
Hey, I saw that Taco Bell is
celebrating its 60th anniversary

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.431
with an all-new vegetarian meal.

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:14.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.735
And actually, it's
the first time anyone's ever

00:02:16.735 --> 00:02:18.938
said "Happy anniversary"
inside a Taco Bell.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.406
-Wow.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.874
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:23.108
-Some TV news.

00:02:23.108 --> 00:02:25.711
CBS is releasing a new
dating competition show

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:28.848
called "The Real Love Boat,"
in which a big group of singles

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.717
spend nearly a
month together on a cruise.

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:31.750
-Ooh.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.052
-Yep, it's the only dating show

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.388
where the winner is
whoever gets kicked off first.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.590
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.158
It's just like "The Bachelor,"

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:41.427
but instead of a rose,
you get a bottle of imodium.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.462
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:46.599 line:0%
And finally, I saw that today
is National Puppy Day.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:51.203 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:52.304
Yep.

00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:53.406
And not surprisingly,

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.340
National Puppy Day
falls on Hump Day.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:56.542
Oh, we have a great show.

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.778
Give it up for The Roots,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:01.414
-♪ We 'bout to rock it ♪

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.082
♪ Hey, yo, we 'bout to rock it,
my favorite cartoon ♪

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.150
♪ After marriage,
the honeymoon ♪

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.153
♪ Well, me, oh, my,
just gag me with a spoon ♪

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.355
♪ And who loves Popeye,
it's Olive ♪

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.557
♪ 'Bout to flow ♪

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:13.559
♪ Chill out,
flying like an Eskimo ♪

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.661
♪ Is a backstage pass
to "The Tonight Show" ♪

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:19.132
Thanks!

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.033
-What a show we have for
you tonight.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:24.703
You know him from the bands
Jonas Brothers and DNCE.

00:03:24.703 --> 00:03:27.006
Now you can see him
as a judge on the new show

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.875
"Becoming a Popstar,"
which premieres tomorrow

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.111
at 10:00 P.M. on MTV.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.480
Joe Jonas is here tonight!

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.681
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:35.681 --> 00:03:37.116
-I love me some Joe Jonas.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:41.654
-Wow. He's the man.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.856
-I love him.
-Yeah.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.558
Plus, he's currently on his

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:49.528
"Gabriel 'Fluffy' Iglesias"
back on world tour,

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:52.632
and he'll be performing stand up
at Dodger Stadium.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:53.799
-Ooh.

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:55.200
-May 6th and 7th.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.902
Gabriel Iglesias is here.

00:03:56.902 --> 00:03:58.104
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah!

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.238
-One of the biggest comedians,

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.340
one of the funniest
comedians out there.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.443
And we've got great music
from Wolf Alice,

00:04:04.443 --> 00:04:05.845
ladies and gentlemen, tonight.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.948
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.920
So, guys, we are smack
in the middle of March Madness.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.656
And every year we pick
a team to root for,

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.558
and this year,
we picked Gonzaga.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.892
Okay?

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.995
So we gave out these rowdy rags
to all the students

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:24.630
that are following
the team around, okay?

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.500
And what we want them to do is,
at a certain point,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.034
just stand up and start
whipping them around

00:04:29.034 --> 00:04:30.569
and do something, you know,
something crazy.

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:32.371
And so, far it's worked.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:33.906
They've won the last two games.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.274
-Ooh.
-Yeah.

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:36.375
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:37.810
I'm just saying.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.645
They were nail biters,
but they did win.

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:40.646
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:42.181
So, now they're
playing tomorrow.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.283
They're playing
the Arkansas Razorbacks.

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:46.619
[ Cheers ]
-Uh-oh.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:47.987
-No. No.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.021
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:50.823
We have to --
I mean, I love them,

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.691
I hope they do well, but --
-But not too well.

00:04:52.691 --> 00:04:54.961
-Not too well. Yeah, exactly.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.863
We want to help Gonzaga
win again, okay?

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.263
But I think
we should switch it up.

00:04:58.263 --> 00:05:00.332
'Cause right now we want 'em
to sing, like --

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:02.601
♪ I'll tell you what I want,
what I really really want ♪

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:04.503
Yeah, I'm changing that up.
-What?

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:05.504
-Basically, here's what
we want them to do.

00:05:05.504 --> 00:05:07.206
Each half is 20 minutes, right?

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:10.076
So when the game clock goes down
to 11:35 --

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.911
that's when
"The Tonight Show" airs --

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:16.382
I want everyone to stand up
and just take their rowdy rags,

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:17.783
and just whip it around.

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:19.685
But I want to, since they're
playing the Arkansas razorbacks,

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:20.920
I think they should go --

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.321
[ To the tune of baby back ribs
commercial ]

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:24.490
♪ Let's beat the Razorbacks,
Razorbacks, Razorbacks ♪

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.493
♪ Let's beat the Razorbacks,
Razorbacks, Razorbacks ♪

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:31.163
♪ We'll beat
the Razorback kids ♪

00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:35.968
♪ Beat the Razorback kids,
beat Arkansas ♪

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:39.806
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:40.973
You're laughing.

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.541
What are you laughing at?

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:44.343
-That seems like a lot.
-Wait, wait --

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:46.078
You think that the students --
-And the harmonies?

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.314
You want 'em to get
the harmonies in there?

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:51.016
-You think the kids won't
stand up at 11:35 --

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:52.018
-Oh, no. They will.

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:53.619
I'm not saying they won't,
but it --

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:54.854
I don't think it'll
sound like that.

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:56.588
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.588 --> 00:05:57.857
-It might be too tricky.

00:05:57.857 --> 00:06:00.226
So at 11:35 --

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:02.328
-11:35.
-Definitely 11:35.

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:05.197
Stand up, and what I would
like you to try --

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:06.299
again, if we can.

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:07.466
Can we see if we can do it?

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:08.835
-Yeah.
-Alright.

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:10.603
And the Arkansas fan,
you don't have to do it.

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:14.507
You can sit in quiet protest.

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:15.908
One, two --

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:18.210
♪ Let's beat the Razorbacks,
Razorbacks, Razorbacks ♪

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.479
♪ Let's beat the Razorbacks,
Razorbacks, Razorbacks ♪

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:23.982
♪ We'll beat
the Razorback kids ♪

00:06:23.982 --> 00:06:25.818
♪ Beat -- ♪
Stop. Just stop.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.052
Stop, stop, stop, stop, stop.

00:06:27.052 --> 00:06:28.254
Absolutely no.

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:29.821
Disaster.

00:06:29.821 --> 00:06:31.190
It's a complete disaster.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.359
-Well, it's a high harmony.
-It's a complete disaster.

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.428
-Get rid of that high harmony.
-They're never going to do it.

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:36.762
[ Laughter ]
-Right.

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:38.196
And somebody's gonna have to
yell "one, two, three,"

00:06:38.196 --> 00:06:39.332
you know what I mean?

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:40.866
-That's it?
-Well, just go, yeah --

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:42.301
-Oh, that's pretty good.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.236
Stan up and go, "one, two,
three," and don't say anything.

00:06:44.236 --> 00:06:46.506
-Yeah. [ Laughter ]

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:47.806
-Yeah.

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:48.774
And then quiet.

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:49.908
-Right.

00:06:49.908 --> 00:06:52.211
-Alright, so at 11:35 --
I'm changing it up.

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:55.748
-So at 11:35, 11:34.
-When it goes down to 11:40,

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.516
and they're like,
"Oh, here it comes --"

00:06:57.516 --> 00:07:00.886
11:37, 11:36, 11:35.

00:07:00.886 --> 00:07:02.954
-Boom.
-Go, "one, two, three!"

00:07:02.954 --> 00:07:05.992
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:10.596
Okay. That's what they'll do.
-There we go.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.531
-Forget about the other one.
It's too confusing.

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:14.867
I apologize. I apologize.

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:16.269
Why would I...

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:18.104
-It was good heart.
-It is tomorrow night.

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:19.438
It's tomorrow night,
they're playing.

00:07:19.438 --> 00:07:20.572
-What time?

00:07:20.572 --> 00:07:22.040
-Uh, you've got to check
your local listings.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.442
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.442 --> 00:07:25.344
-I think tomorrow, uh -- do
we know what time they play?

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:26.979
-7:00.
-7:00.

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:28.748
-Ooh.
-On the dot.

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.382
But "at 7:00" doesn't mean
anything to me,

00:07:30.382 --> 00:07:33.452
'cause it's when the clock
goes down to 11:35.

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:34.887
-Each?
-Each half.

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:36.555
-Yes.
-You got two opportunities.

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:39.459
Students, if you're rooting
for your team, Gonzaga,

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:40.959
if you're rooting for
the Bulldogs,

00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:47.400
I want you to go, 11:36, 11:35,
"One, two, three!"

00:07:49.201 --> 00:07:50.870
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:54.506
Look at your phone.

00:07:54.506 --> 00:07:57.175
Look at your phone or something,
do whatever you want.

00:07:57.175 --> 00:07:59.979
Act like -- yeah, exactly.
That's what I want.

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:01.480
-And then imaginarily
talk to somebody.

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:03.148
-And go Zags.
Go Zags, everybody.

00:08:03.148 --> 00:08:04.550
We got this, come on.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:05.584
[ Cheers and applause ]
We got this.

00:08:05.584 --> 00:08:09.121
Sweet Sixteen, baby.

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:13.626
Guys, I have a book coming out,
called "Nana Loves You More."

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:14.694
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:17.730
I'm very excited about this.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:21.834
This one's $17.99.

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:23.169
-Ooh.
-Yeah.

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:25.271
$1,799.
-Wow, okay.

00:08:25.271 --> 00:08:26.706
[ Laughter ]

00:08:26.706 --> 00:08:29.074
-Look at what you get here.
-That's a lot of pages, yeah.

00:08:29.074 --> 00:08:30.275
-Look at this thickness.

00:08:30.275 --> 00:08:31.310
And in there --

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:34.246
But in this series,
you have Dada,

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:35.781
you have Mama, Baby, Nana.

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:37.049
But I'm going to get into it.

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:39.719
I wanted to have a theme week,
a Nana theme week.

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:42.922
Next week is all, we're gonna
celebrate grandmas

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:45.824
around the country,
and we love grandmas.

00:08:45.824 --> 00:08:47.994
And so, check our socials.

00:08:47.994 --> 00:08:50.863
We might need
your grandmas to participate

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:52.531
and do something fun
for our show.

00:08:52.531 --> 00:08:55.167
So, check the @Fallontonight
or @Jimmyfallon.

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:56.202
That's gonna be fun.

00:08:56.202 --> 00:09:00.839
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:00.839 --> 00:09:02.541
Yeah, that was a bad idea.

00:09:02.541 --> 00:09:03.676
Alright, so, good.

00:09:03.676 --> 00:09:04.977
Do "one, two, three," silence.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:07.079
-Silence.
-Yeah, perfect.

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:08.314
God, there's so much going on.

00:09:08.314 --> 00:09:09.915
Did you guys hear
about the Volkswagen recall?

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:11.016
-Oh.

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:12.818
-It's not good.
Here, check this out.

00:09:12.818 --> 00:09:15.954 line:0%
-A concerning recall alert,
impacting thousands of drivers.

00:09:15.954 --> 00:09:19.391 line:0%
Volkswagen recalling more than
200,00 SUVs in the US.

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:22.060 line:0%
Reports found faulty wiring
could cause problems

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:23.963 line:0%
with airbags,
windows, and brakes.

00:09:23.963 --> 00:09:25.531 line:0%
-What? What?

00:09:25.531 --> 00:09:26.666
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:29.435
Aw, man, I just bought
a Volkswagen SUV.

00:09:29.435 --> 00:09:31.470
-Oh, sorry about that, Tariq.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.571
-It's okay.

00:09:32.571 --> 00:09:35.041
I still have my trusty Kia.

00:09:35.041 --> 00:09:36.709
I love that car.

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:38.243
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:38.243 --> 00:09:39.378
-Oh.

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:40.479
[ Laughter ]

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:41.947
